※ pl4g-test: module
※※ Bundles a program beside this one applies.

※ Exported, so a file importing this one may apply it.  What it applies in turn
※ is this file's own, which a file applying `number` cannot name and does not
※ need to: a bundle's lines are read with the names its own file can see.
@[export]
bundle number(T'):
    addable(T')
    T' ⌈ T' → T'

bundle addable(T'):  T' ⊞ T' → T'

※ Not exported, and what it names is not exported either: a bundle is checked
※ where it was written, so it may require an operation the file applying it
※ cannot name at all.
@[export]
bundle steppable(T'):  step(T') → T'

fn step(a: u8) → u8:
    a ⊞ 1u8
